      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "tACK 64cf455b48\r\n\r\nTested on macOS 27.0.1 (Apple Silicon arm64).\r\nrpc_getblockfilter.py passes.\r\nReplacing if (!block_was_connected) with if (block_was_connected) in getblockfilter in src/rpc/blockchain.cpp makes the PR's test fail, while the test from master 6c01bd0b2d still passes with the same mutation:\r\n\r\nExpected: Filter not found. Block was not connected to active chain.\r\nActual:   Filter not found. This error is unexpected and indicates index corruption.\r\nThe code implies that the header-only block has not reached BLOCK_VALID_SCRIPTS on node 0, so the new assertion exercises the intended -5 error path.",
